== at 600 x 400, with 20 points of padding ==
  the screen's box is the window: true
  the card's box is the window less the padding: true
  which is not what viewport() would have said: true
  cw(5) is a share of the box: true
  a share under the floor is the floor: true
  and one over the ceiling is the ceiling: true
  and the card heard its layout: true
  reading the box is the declaration: true
  the one that never read it does not follow: true
== dragged to 400 x 300 ==
  the card's box moved, so it asks to render: true
  and the quiet one does not: true
  on_layout ran again: true
  its box is the new window less the padding: true
  and cw(5) followed it down: true
== a box that decides itself ==
  is refused rather than laid out for ever: true
  and the message says what is still moving: true
